        <section id="detailed_desc">
            <p>When the state of the media player changes, the SDK triggers this callback to report the current playback state.</p>
            <p props="android">For on-demand playback, <ph keyref="PLAYER_STATE_PLAYBACK_COMPLETED" /> (5) indicates that the current playback has completed and the player will continue repeating. <ph keyref="PLAYER_STATE_PLAYBACK_ALL_LOOPS_COMPLETED" /> (6) indicates that the final playback has completed.</p>
            <p props="android">Handle <ph keyref="PLAYER_STATE_PLAYBACK_ALL_LOOPS_COMPLETED" /> (6) when the entire playback session completes normally. This state is also reported after a single playback when looping is not configured. Each playback iteration reports only one completion state; the final iteration reports <ph keyref="PLAYER_STATE_PLAYBACK_ALL_LOOPS_COMPLETED" /> (6) without first reporting <ph keyref="PLAYER_STATE_PLAYBACK_COMPLETED" /> (5).</p>
        </section>
        <section id="playback_scenarios" props="android">
            <title>On-demand playback scenarios</title>
            <p>Only playback-completion and stop states are listed. Intermediate states such as opening and playing are omitted.</p>
